.TH "REPROCTL\-START" "1" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
reproctl\-start \- start services via Tilt
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]reproctl start\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-wait\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-timeout\f[R]
\f[I]duration\f[R]] \f[I]service\f[R] [\f[I]service\f[R]...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Start one or more services from the current context (main checkout or
worktree).
.PP
Service names are validated against the project\(aqs
\f[B]services.json\f[R] manifest.
The requested services are written to \f[B]reproctl_services.json\f[R],
which the Tiltfile reads to determine which resources to enable.
.PP
If the Tilt daemon is not already running, it is started automatically.
.PP
When invoked from a worktree, services are isolated with a
worktree\-slug suffix so they do not conflict with services running from
the main checkout or other worktrees.
.PP
If no service names are provided and stdin is a terminal, an interactive
picker is shown (using \f[B]fzf\f[R] if available, or a numbered
prompt).
.PP
The available service list in \f[B]reproctl start \-\-help\f[R] is
generated directly from \f[B]infra/services.json\f[R], so new services
appear automatically without shell\-script changes.
.PP
For extension verification, \f[CR]reproctl start \-\-wait capture\f[R]
or \f[CR]reproctl start \-\-wait dev\-toolbar\f[R] is the standard prep
step before \f[CR]agent\-browser\f[R] attaches to the isolated browser
session.
Shared browser profiles, auth, and cache live under
\f[CR]/Users/gary/Projects/repro\-dev/repro/tmp/agent\-browser/\f[R],
while screenshots, notes, logs, and disposable profile overrides stay
under the worktree
\f[CR]tmp/extension\-verification/<issue\-or\-surface>/...\f[R] tree.
This brings up the extension build/watch pipeline and any required local
services before browser automation begins.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-\-pick\f[R], \f[B]\-p\f[R]
Interactively select a service.
Uses \f[B]fzf\f[R] if installed, otherwise a numbered prompt.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-wait\f[R], \f[B]\-w\f[R]
Block until all started services report healthy status.
While waiting, the full transitive dependency tree is resolved from
\f[B]services.json\f[R] and the status of all dependencies
(infrastructure, migrations, dependent services) is shown alongside the
target services.
In a TTY, a multi\-line updating display is shown on stderr.
When not a TTY, periodic single\-line status updates are printed to
stderr every 10 seconds.
Exits 0 on success, 1 on timeout.
In \f[B]\-\-json\f[R] mode, outputs the final service status JSON on
success, or an error object on timeout.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-timeout\f[R], \f[B]\-t\f[R] \f[I]duration\f[R]
How long to wait before giving up when \f[B]\-\-wait\f[R] is set.
Accepts a number of seconds, optionally with an \f[B]s\f[R] suffix (e.g.
\f[B]120s\f[R], \f[B]60\f[R]).
By default, \f[B]\-\-wait\f[R] blocks indefinitely with no timeout.
Only meaningful with \f[B]\-\-wait\f[R].
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
\f[B]0\f[R]
Services started successfully (and healthy, if \f[B]\-\-wait\f[R] was
used).
.TP
\f[B]1\f[R]
Error, or timeout when waiting for services.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
reproctl start api\-server
Start the api\-server from the current context.
.TP
reproctl start api\-server workspace
Start multiple services at once.
.TP
reproctl start \-\-wait api\-server
Start the api\-server and block until it is healthy.
Shows database, storage, and migration dependency status while waiting.
.TP
reproctl start \-\-wait capture
Prepare the capture\-extension workflow by waiting for the extension
build/watch pipeline and local dependencies to become healthy.
Use the main\-checkout \f[CR]tmp/agent\-browser/\f[R] tree for shared
browser state and the worktree
\f[CR]tmp/extension\-verification/<issue\-or\-surface>/\f[R] tree for
screenshots and notes.
.TP
reproctl start \-\-wait dev\-toolbar
Prepare the Dev Toolbar extension workflow by waiting for the extension
build/watch pipeline and local dependencies to become healthy.
Use the main\-checkout \f[CR]tmp/agent\-browser/\f[R] tree for shared
browser state and the worktree
\f[CR]tmp/extension\-verification/<issue\-or\-surface>/\f[R] tree for
screenshots and notes.
.TP
reproctl start \-\-wait \-\-timeout 60s api\-server workspace
Start services and wait up to 60 seconds for all to become healthy.
.TP
reproctl \-\-json start \-\-wait api\-server
Start the api\-server, wait for healthy, and output final status as
JSON.
